.PP
The cell width is \f[CR]term_cols / ncols\f[R] minus the separator.
Tail column is data\-driven (capped at ⅓ of cell).
Long descriptions are truncated, so a verbose binding can\[cq]t blow out
the column alignment.
.SH Limitations
.IP \[bu] 2
Uses \f[CR]E.status_msg\f[R] (4 KB), so very large keymaps may overflow
at the highest column counts.
The display caps at \f[CR]MAX_LINES *   ncols\f[R] cells.
.IP \[bu] 2
Not a real buffer \[em] no scrolling, no syntax highlighting, no
selection.
If a generic \[lq]bottom panel\[rq] plugin extension point is ever
added, whichkey is the obvious candidate to migrate.
.IP \[bu] 2
Renders immediately on every keystroke; no configurable delay.
The chord timeout (5 s) is the only knob.
